# The ONE motir-core origin every cross-origin door on the landing is built
# from (MOTIR-1152). Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development.
#
# ⚠️ IT IS READ AT BUILD TIME, NOT AT RUNTIME. `PUBLIC_*` values are
# INLINED into the pages by `astro build`, so setting this on the deployed
# Worker would do nothing for them — they were built without it. CI's
# workflow-level `env` sets the production value for the `Build` check and the
# release alike; the Worker's live pages read `wrangler.jsonc`'s
# `MOTIR_APP_ORIGIN` instead.
#
# `lib/appOrigin.ts` throws `MotirAppOriginError` when it is missing or is not
# a bare http(s) origin, which fails the build with the variable's name rather
# than shipping three dead doors.
PUBLIC_MOTIR_APP_ORIGIN=https://app.motir.co

# motir-ai's public origin (MOTIR-8382): /price reads its plan ladder and the
# calculator from it. Same build-time rule. `lib/aiOrigin.ts` never throws,
# but unset, the pages built from the plan ladder (/price,
# /how-the-calculation-works) stop the build rather than ship without figures
# (MOTIR-10644).
PUBLIC_MOTIR_AI_ORIGIN=https://ai.motir.co

# ── The entity signal (MOTIR-1154) ──────────────────────────────────────────

# THIS site's own public origin — what `metadataBase`, the canonical, the
# sitemap's entries, `robots.txt`'s `sitemap:` line and every `url` / `@id` in
# the JSON-LD graph are built from. It has a DEFAULT (`https://motir.co`), so
# leaving it unset is the normal case and every build works with no
# configuration; set it only for a deployment that should advertise a different
# origin, such as a preview.
#
# ⚠️ SAME BUILD-TIME RULE AS THE VARIABLE ABOVE. It is `PUBLIC_*` and every
# consumer is statically rendered, so it is INLINED by `astro build`. Override
# it in the build's environment, as the app origin is; the Worker's live pages
# read `wrangler.jsonc`'s `MOTIR_SITE_ORIGIN` instead.
#
# `lib/siteOrigin.ts` throws `MotirSiteOriginError` when it is SET but is not a
# bare http(s) origin. An unset value is not an error; a typo is.
# PUBLIC_MOTIR_SITE_ORIGIN=https://motir.co

# The Google Search Console HTML-tag verification token, rendered as
# `<meta name="google-site-verification">` by the root metadata.
#
# ⚠️ DELIBERATELY UNSET, AND THAT IS THE FINISHED STATE — not a value waiting to
# be filled in. `motir.co` is verified in Search Console as a DOMAIN property,
# by DNS (MOTIR-1155, 2026-08-27), which covers the apex and every subdomain and
# issues NO meta-tag token: the `google-site-verification=` string that method
# produces is a TXT record VALUE and is not interchangeable with this one. The
# root metadata omits the tag entirely when this is unset, which is correct. Do NOT create a
# second URL-prefix property to manufacture a token — the Domain property
# supersedes one, and a second property fragments the reporting.
#
# It is read at BUILD time (the root metadata is a static export on a statically
# rendered route), so if it is ever set it goes in the build's own environment
# like the origins above (CI's workflow-level `env`), never on the deployed
# Worker, where the already-built pages would never read it.
# MOTIR_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=
